==Trivia==
*In real life, a [[wikipedia:Stellar corona|corona]] is an aura of plasma that surrounds the Sun and other stars.
**''Corona'' is also a Latin word, translating to 'garland, wreath, crown'.
*Corona is a reference to idol and model [[wikipedia:Yuko Ogura|Yuko Ogura]], who often jokingly claims to be one "Princess Apple-Momoka" (りんごももか姫) of the apple-shaped planet Korin. Case in point, Corona is an apple-shaped planet on the [[Cats of the Cosmos]] map, its Japanese name is Planet Koron, its [[Treasure]] is a pop idol, and its base is adorned with apples and a symbol of a peach (''momo'' means peach).
*In May 2010, a space probe called [[wikipedia:Akatsuki (spacecraft)|Akatsuki]] was launched from Japan towards Venus. A signature petition resulted in images of the Vocaloid [[Hatsune Miku Collaboration Event|Hatsune Miku]] being placed onboard the spacecraft. Since Venus happens to have coronae, this might be why the figure on the enemy base looks so much like Hatsune Miku.

